# M6 walkthrough: a coder with a sandbox, and the task's files.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisites: a default model (m1-providers.http), and the runner: `pnpm stack:up`, or in dev
# `docker compose --profile app build sandbox-dev` once, then `pnpm dev:runner` next to `pnpm dev`.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@departmentId = paste-a-department-id
@taskId = paste-a-task-id

### A department of engineers: a lead...
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "eng-lead",
  "name": "Engineering lead",
  "role": "lead",
  "departmentId": "{{departmentId}}",
  "description": "Plans engineering work and reports results.",
  "instructions": "Delegate coding to the coder, then report what it found."
}

### ...and a coder with a workspace: files to read and write, a shell to run commands.
### Add "requireApproval": true to a grant to approve each change or command (GET /v1/attention).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "coder",
  "name": "Coder",
  "role": "specialist",
  "departmentId": "{{departmentId}}",
  "description": "Writes programs in its workspace and runs them.",
  "instructions": "Write the code to a file, run it, and return the exact output.",
  "tools": [{ "key": "files" }, { "key": "shell" }]
}

### Some work: the coder gets the task's sandbox (no network; Node, Python and git inside)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "departmentId": "{{departmentId}}",
  "title": "First primes",
  "brief": "Write primes.py that prints the first 10 prime numbers, run it, and report the output."
}

### What it wrote
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}/files?depth=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Download a file (slashes plain or encoded: src/main.py or src%2Fmain.py)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}/files/primes.py
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sandboxes: idle ones stop after 15 minutes, stopped ones go after 7 days; files stay
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/sandboxes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Remove one now (its next command starts a fresh one, with the same files)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/sandboxes/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
